ey ($322K) and a well-funded challenger, but Carey holds a large cash edge"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican hold: a +5 Republican district, an incumbent with a big fundraising advantage, and a ratings consensus of Likely R. The recent Democratic-sponsored poll showing a one-point race and outside attacks on Carey over SNAP and Medicaid cuts justify moving a few points toward the Democrat, but prediction markets still price Carey near 74%.", "watch": "Any independent (non-sponsored) polling confirming the late-September tightening, or further outside spending into the district, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 15th District, a Republican-leaning seat around Columbus, features incumbent Mike Carey facing Democrat Don Leonard and a Libertarian candidate. Carey has out-raised Leonard by more than five to one and holds a large cash advantage, though Democratic outside groups have spent over $300,000 attacking him over cuts to SNAP, Medicaid, and education. National Democrats have targeted the district with advertising.\n\nMost race raters call this Likely Republican, with a couple at Lean Republican and one at Tossup. The only recent polling is Democratic-sponsored and shows a very close race, a notable shift from earlier summer surveys. Prediction markets still favor Carey by roughly three to one. The seat leans Republican, but the race appears closer than a typical incumbent hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1541, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1445, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1885, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "